Authoritative feature evidence and limits for this experiment:
{"facts":[{"id":"cal-ai-methods","statement":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description","sourceUrl":"https://www.calai.app/"},{"id":"cal-ai-recipes","statement":"Add custom foods and recipes","sourceUrl":"https://www.calai.app/"},{"id":"cal-ai-estimates","statement":"Nutrition estimates vary; clear focused photos and good lighting help scans, but do not ensure exactness","sourceUrl":"https://www.calai.app/"}],"claimsToAvoid":["Exact or perfectly accurate calorie counts","Guaranteed weight loss or health results","Fabricated transformations","A specific amount of time saved"],"testimonialEvidence":[],"limitations":"Cal AI is a calorie and nutrient logging app. Users can photograph a meal, scan a barcode or describe food. Users can also add their own foods and recipes. Photo analysis is about 80% accurate and nutrition values can vary; good lighting and a clearly focused food or label can help the scan. It does not guarantee exact calorie counts, weight loss or health results. No personal transformation or testimonial is supplied."}
Choose the lesson before prose. Use this pre-generated plan corresponding to each candidate slot; preserve the assigned format and existing word/layout rules:
{"lessons":[{"slot":0,"problem":"Logging meals can be a source of stress rather than support.","mistakenAssumption":"Meal logging has to be time-consuming and complicated.","lesson":"Using convenient meal tracking methods can help reduce stress.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods"],"productMechanism":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description","practicalAction":"Try taking a quick photo of your meal instead of writing it down later.","takeaway":"Simplifying the logging process can alleviate the pressure of tracking meals.","limitations":"Photo analysis accuracy can vary, and it may not capture every detail."},{"slot":1,"problem":"Family meals complicate personal meal logging.","mistakenAssumption":"You need to log every meal precisely to maintain a healthy diet.","lesson":"Multiple logging methods can simplify tracking amidst busy family life.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods","cal-ai-recipes"],"productMechanism":"Add custom foods and recipes","practicalAction":"Log your family's meal by scanning the barcode of a shared dish or taking a photo.","takeaway":"Flexibility in logging can help you manage both family and personal nutrition.","limitations":"Nutrition estimates can vary, and not every family meal may have a barcode."},{"slot":2,"problem":"Relying on estimates can create uncertainty about progress.","mistakenAssumption":"All meal logging methods provide equally accurate calorie counts.","lesson":"Understanding the variability in estimates can help users make better choices.","factIds":["cal-ai-estimates"],"productMechanism":"Nutrition estimates vary; clear focused photos and good lighting help scans, but do not ensure exactness","practicalAction":"When entering a homemade recipe, consider using a clear photo for better accuracy.","takeaway":"Being aware of potential inaccuracies can help you make informed dietary choices.","limitations":"Nutrition estimates may still not reflect exact values."},{"slot":3,"problem":"Choosing how to log meals can feel overwhelming.","mistakenAssumption":"You must choose the most accurate method every time you log a meal.","lesson":"Offering multiple input methods can alleviate decision fatigue.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods"],"productMechanism":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description","practicalAction":"Experiment with different logging methods, like taking a photo or scanning a barcode, to see which feels easiest.","takeaway":"Flexibility in how you log meals can make the process less daunting.","limitations":"Some methods may require more effort than others depending on the situation."},{"slot":4,"problem":"The guilt of missing a log can overshadow healthy intentions.","mistakenAssumption":"You must log every calorie to be successful in weight management.","lesson":"Understanding that flexibility in logging can support a balanced approach.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods"],"productMechanism":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description","practicalAction":"If you forget to log a meal, don’t stress; just log the next one using a quick photo.","takeaway":"It's okay to have flexibility in your logging; it can lead to a healthier mindset.","limitations":"Missing logs may still affect overall tracking accuracy."}]}

